    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 48 tests pass, including the new `Cp35Tests`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for `POST /api/owners`. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it's still created and flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two read-only fields to the `Owner` DTO schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32, present only when the flag is true).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) columns with getters/setters, mirroring the existing snapshot-at-creation fields like `namesakeCount`. MapStruct auto-maps them by name into the DTO.\n\n3. **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` and `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new function class) \u2014 a pipeline step that, on the built owner, finds an existing owner with matching `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` but a different `telephone`; sets `possibleDuplicate=true` / `possibleDuplicateOf=<lowest matching id>` when found, otherwise `false`. It skips when the new owner has no postcode and never matches itself.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignPossibleDuplicate` step (under `transaction` governance) between the hard-duplicate `checkIdentityUnique` check and `assignCustomerCode`, so the flag is computed only after a hard duplicate has been ruled out and before the owner is saved.\n\nThe full acceptance suite (48 tests, including the new `Cp35Tests`) is green.",
